{"id":"q53","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"fact","question":"Was the Declaration of Independence signed by most of its signers on July 4, 1776?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The Declaration is dated July 4, 1776, because Congress approved the final text that day.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.3,"theta":1.4137,"phi":1.3541},{"text":"Hancock and Charles Thomson are generally believed to have signed the printed copy on July 4.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.3,"theta":0.9425,"phi":0.446},{"text":"The July 4 date is strongly associated with the document in popular memory.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.2566,"phi":1.1236},{"text":"Most signers did not sign on July 4.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.0964},{"text":"The engrossed parchment copy was prepared after July 4.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.0605},{"text":"Most delegates signed the engrossed copy on August 2, 1776.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.0724},{"text":"Some signers were not present on August 2 and signed later.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.0986},{"text":"Matthew Thornton signed in November 1776.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1097},{"text":"The date on the document reflects adoption of the text, not when most signatures were applied.","confidence":0.92,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4451,"phi":2.6671},{"text":"The claim that most signers signed on July 4 is false.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1057}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":9,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":8,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":5,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":